"use strict";(self.webpackChunkseriousjul_github_io=self.webpackChunkseriousjul_github_io||[]).push([["602"],{5272(e){e.exports=JSON.parse('{"archive":{"blogPosts":[{"id":"2026-10-18-egui-egui-0370-emoji-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-egui-egui-0370-emoji-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-10-18-egui-egui-0370-emoji-release.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-18-egui-egui-0370-emoji-release.mdx","title":"Egui 0.37.0 lands colored emoji support","description":"Egui 0.37.0, titled \\"Colored emojis!\\", was released on 2026-10-15 and is the first release to ship full emoji and glyph support via a new glyph rasterizer and font provider API. The same release adds a CompletionPopup autocomplete widget and an experimental theme plugin system, alongside improved AccessKit accessibility, video recording of integration tests, and breaking changes for API users.","date":"2026-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"egui","permalink":"/news/tags/egui","description":"Posts about the egui GUI framework"}],"readingTime":1.23,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Egui 0.37.0 lands colored emoji support","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","egui"],"slug":"2026-10-18-egui-egui-0370-emoji-release"},"unlisted":false,"nextItem":{"title":"n8n 2.43.7 stable lands execution suspension as ZoomInfo ships native node","permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration"}},"content":"Egui 0.37.0, titled \\"Colored emojis!\\", was released on 2026-10-15 and is the first release to ship full emoji and glyph support via a new glyph rasterizer and font provider API. The same release adds a CompletionPopup autocomplete widget and an experimental theme plugin system, alongside improved AccessKit accessibility, video recording of integration tests, and breaking changes for API users.\\n\\n## Releases\\n- On 2026-10-15, egui released stable version 0.37.0 (\\"Colored emojis!\\") featuring full emoji and glyph support through a new glyph rasterizer/font provider API, a CompletionPopup autocomplete widget, an experimental theme plugin system, improved AccessKit accessibility, and video recording of integration tests ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n\\n## Features\\n- Full colored emoji and glyph support via a new glyph rasterizer and font provider API, introduced in 0.37.0 on 2026-10-15 ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n- New CompletionPopup autocomplete widget in 0.37.0, released 2026-10-15 ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n- Experimental theme plugin system shipped in 0.37.0 on 2026-10-15 ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n- Improved accessibility through AccessKit and video recording of integration tests, both in 0.37.0 on 2026-10-15 ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n\\n## Fixes and other\\n- Breaking changes in 0.37.0 (2026-10-15): the AsId trait was removed and default_fonts was dropped from the default feature set ([source](https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0)).\\n\\n## Sources\\n- https://github.com/emilk/egui/releases/tag/0.37.0"},{"id":"2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration.mdx","title":"n8n 2.43.7 stable lands execution suspension as ZoomInfo ships native node","description":"n8n shipped four releases between Oct 14 and Oct 16, led by stable 2.43.7, which can now suspend in-flight production executions when a worker shuts down. The biggest ecosystem news came from ZoomInfo, which launched a verified native n8n node exposing its GTM Context Graph for workflows and AI agents.","date":"2026-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"n8n","permalink":"/news/tags/n8n","description":"Posts about the n8n workflow automation tool"}],"readingTime":1.73,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"n8n 2.43.7 stable lands execution suspension as ZoomInfo ships native node","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","n8n"],"slug":"2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Egui 0.37.0 lands colored emoji support","permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-egui-egui-0370-emoji-release"},"nextItem":{"title":"Omarchy 4.0.5 ships Qt 6.12 and BORE-scheduler kernel","permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release"}},"content":"n8n shipped four releases between Oct 14 and Oct 16, led by stable 2.43.7, which can now suspend in-flight production executions when a worker shuts down. The biggest ecosystem news came from ZoomInfo, which launched a verified native n8n node exposing its GTM Context Graph for workflows and AI agents.\\n\\n## Releases\\n\\n- 2026-10-16: n8n 2.43.7 (latest stable) released, adding the ability to suspend in-flight production executions at worker shutdown in core. [Release](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.7)\\n- 2026-10-15: n8n 2.43.6 released with a core fix creating a fresh XML parser for each webhook request body. [Release](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.6)\\n- 2026-10-14: n8n 2.43.5 released, showing Gemini models by name and listing prioritized models first in model pickers. [Release](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.5)\\n- 2026-10-14: n8n 1.123.85, a routine maintenance release for the legacy 1.x branch with no notable changes listed. [Release](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%401.123.85)\\n\\n## Features\\n\\n- 2026-10-12: ZoomInfo announced a native, verified ZoomInfo node inside n8n, built and maintained by ZoomInfo. Once a workflow authenticates with a customer\'s own ZoomInfo credentials, it can search contacts and companies, enrich records, and monitor buying-signal and intent data from ZoomInfo\'s GTM Context Graph via GTM.AI. [Announcement](https://ir.zoominfo.com/news-releases/news-release-details/zoominfo-launches-native-integration-n8n-through-gtmai/)\\n\\n## Fixes and other\\n\\n- 2026-10-15: Webhook XML parsing fixed in 2.43.6 by creating a fresh XML parser for each request body. [Release](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.6)\\n- 2026-10-14: chunk() expression extension now validates its size argument, shipped in 2.43.5. [Release](https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.5)\\n\\n## Sources\\n\\n- https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.7\\n- https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.6\\n- https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%402.43.5\\n- https://github.com/n8n-io/n8n/releases/tag/n8n%401.123.85\\n- https://ir.zoominfo.com/news-releases/news-release-details/zoominfo-launches-native-integration-n8n-through-gtmai/"},{"id":"2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release.mdx","title":"Omarchy 4.0.5 ships Qt 6.12 and BORE-scheduler kernel","description":"Omarchy 4.0.5 was released on 18 October 2026 as a stable point release bringing fixes and refinements ahead of the next feature release. The update moves the distro onto the Qt 6.12 toolkit, bumps stable-ring packages, and ships an updated Linux 7.2 stable kernel with the BORE scheduler. Phoronix also covered the release, highlighting millisecond-level optimization of web browser launch by avoiding XDG overhead.","date":"2026-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Omarchy","permalink":"/news/tags/omarchy","description":"Posts about the Omarchy Linux distribution"}],"readingTime":1.2,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Omarchy 4.0.5 ships Qt 6.12 and BORE-scheduler kernel","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","omarchy"],"slug":"2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"n8n 2.43.7 stable lands execution suspension as ZoomInfo ships native node","permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-n8n-n8n-2-43-7-zoominfo-integration"},"nextItem":{"title":"Strata 0.1.45 adds picture reading and parallel serving","permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-strata-strata-0145-parallel-speedups"}},"content":"Omarchy 4.0.5 was released on 18 October 2026 as a stable point release bringing fixes and refinements ahead of the next feature release. The update moves the distro onto the Qt 6.12 toolkit, bumps stable-ring packages, and ships an updated Linux 7.2 stable kernel with the BORE scheduler. Phoronix also covered the release, highlighting millisecond-level optimization of web browser launch by avoiding XDG overhead.\\n\\n## Releases\\n- v4.0.5 (stable) released on 18 Oct 2026, with a set of fixes and refinements, a move to Qt 6.12, stable-ring package bumps, and an updated kernel with the BORE scheduler; existing machines can upgrade via Update > Omarchy and new installs use the 4.0.5 ISO ([GitHub release](https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/releases/tag/v4.0.5))\\n\\n## Features\\n- Faster default web browser launch via millisecond-level optimization that avoids the xdg-settings get default-web-browser overhead, as reported on the 4.0.5 release (18 Oct 2026) ([Phoronix](https://www.phoronix.com/news/Omarchy-Faster-Web-Browser))\\n\\n## Fixes and other\\n- Improved reliability of Wi-Fi QR code generation among other fixes in v4.0.5 (18 Oct 2026) ([GitHub release](https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/releases/tag/v4.0.5))\\n\\n## Community\\n- Phoronix (Michael Larabel) covered the 4.0.5 release on 18 Oct 2026, noting it pulls in the Linux 7.2 stable kernel with BORE scheduler and Qt 6.12 updates alongside smaller improvements ([Phoronix](https://www.phoronix.com/news/Omarchy-Faster-Web-Browser))\\n\\n## Sources\\n- https://github.com/omacom/omarchy/releases/tag/v4.0.5\\n- https://www.phoronix.com/news/Omarchy-Faster-Web-Browser"},{"id":"2026-10-18-strata-strata-0145-parallel-speedups","metadata":{"permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-strata-strata-0145-parallel-speedups","editUrl":"https://github.com/SeriousJul/seriousjul.github.io/tree/main/blog/2026-10-18-strata-strata-0145-parallel-speedups.mdx","source":"@site/blog/2026-10-18-strata-strata-0145-parallel-speedups.mdx","title":"Strata 0.1.45 adds picture reading and parallel serving","description":"Strata v0.1.45 shipped on October 17, 2026, bringing picture reading to Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, concurrent request serving via --parallel (up to ~40% faster on tested GPUs), and opt-in switches for multi-user servers. Qwen3.8-Flash-Next answers remain byte-identical to 0.1.44.1. A r/LocalLLaMA thread also discussed Qwen3.8-Flash-Next with user reports of testing Strata.","date":"2026-10-18T00:00:00.000Z","tags":[{"inline":false,"label":"Project","permalink":"/news/tags/project","description":"Posts about projects and their releases"},{"inline":false,"label":"Strata","permalink":"/news/tags/strata","description":"Posts about the Strata local LLM engine"}],"readingTime":1.95,"hasTruncateMarker":false,"authors":[{"name":"Julien Antony","title":"Systems tinkerer","url":"https://seriousjul.github.io","page":{"permalink":"/news/authors/seriousjul"},"socials":{"github":"https://github.com/seriousjul"},"imageURL":"https://github.com/seriousjul.png","key":"seriousjul"}],"frontMatter":{"title":"Strata 0.1.45 adds picture reading and parallel serving","authors":["seriousjul"],"tags":["project","strata"],"slug":"2026-10-18-strata-strata-0145-parallel-speedups"},"unlisted":false,"prevItem":{"title":"Omarchy 4.0.5 ships Qt 6.12 and BORE-scheduler kernel","permalink":"/news/2026-10-18-omarchy-omarchy-4-0-5-release"}},"content":"Strata v0.1.45 shipped on October 17, 2026, bringing picture reading to Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, concurrent request serving via --parallel (up to ~40% faster on tested GPUs), and opt-in switches for multi-user servers. Qwen3.8-Flash-Next answers remain byte-identical to 0.1.44.1. A r/LocalLLaMA thread also discussed Qwen3.8-Flash-Next with user reports of testing Strata.\\n\\n## Releases\\n- **v0.1.45 released (2026-10-17)**: picture reading for Qwen3.6-35B-A3B, several concurrent requests at once, up to 40% faster runs on tested GPUs, switches for multi-user servers, and Mac and setup fixes. Update via `UPDATE.bat` (Linux: `./update.sh`); setup replaces the engine with 0.1.45. ([Source](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45))\\n\\n## Features\\n- **Picture support for Qwen3.6-35B-A3B (v0.1.45, 2026-10-17)**: setup asks \\"Do you want images?\\" for Qwen3.6, downloads the pinned mmproj (~0.9 GB) and writes `--vision`; it uses the same image encoder family as Flash-Next, and output was checked against llama.cpp on the same pictures with teacher forcing. ([Source](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45))\\n- **Concurrent requests (v0.1.45, 2026-10-17)**: the server now handles several requests at once via `--parallel` (up to 8 slots per the release notes), running up to ~40% faster on the GPUs tested. ([Source](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45))\\n- **Multi-user server switches (v0.1.45, 2026-10-17)**: opt-in switches for running multi-user servers were added. ([Source](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45))\\n\\n## Fixes and other\\n- **Mac and setup fixes (v0.1.45, 2026-10-17)**: routine Mac and setup fixes are bundled in the release. ([Source](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45))\\n- **Identity guarantee for Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (v0.1.45, 2026-10-17)**: answers of the Qwen3.8-Flash-Next models are byte-identical to 0.1.44.1 in the project\'s identity tests on every GPU machine tested (CUDA sm_60 / sm_86, HIP gfx1201, Intel A750, Mac M4). ([Source](https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45))\\n\\n## Community\\n- **r/LocalLLaMA thread on Qwen3.8-Flash-Next (2026-10-16)**: the discussion thread \\"I don\'t get the qwen 3.8 flash next hype\\" includes user reports of testing the model with Strata, with one user saying Strata results were worse than llama.cpp on their 4x 3090 setup despite faster generation. ([Source](https://www.reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/comments/1x7uf15/i_dont_get_the_qwen_38_flash_next_hype/))\\n\\n## Sources\\n- https://github.com/Niko1221/Strata/releases/tag/v0.1.45\\n- https://www.reddit.com/r/LocalLLaMA/comments/1x7uf15/i_dont_get_the_qwen_38_flash_next_hype/"}]}}')}}]);